+``mediacodec`` (Android)
+    Renders ``IMGFMT_MEDIACODEC`` frames directly to an ``android.view.Surface``
+    with per-frame presentation timestamps, and renders subtitles/OSD into a
+    second, transparent ``android.view.Surface``. Requires
+    ``--wid=(intptr_t)(*android.view.Surface)`` and, for OSD/subtitles,
+    ``--vo-mediacodec-osd-surface=(intptr_t)(*android.view.Surface)``.
+    Hardware sessions require ``--hwdec=mediacodec`` (not ``-copy``); software
+    frames are rejected, since copying them in would connect the Surface as a
+    CPU producer and prevent a GL VO from binding it later.
+
+    The embedder owns geometry: the video Surface must be sized to the
+    aspect-corrected video rectangle (decoded buffers are scaled to the whole
+    Surface), and the OSD Surface must be placed directly above it with the
+    same bounds. Since decoded buffers go straight to the system compositor,
+    the decoder's dataspace (HDR) is preserved and no GPU pass runs, but
+    video filters and screenshots are unavailable.
+
+    On Android 11+ the driver also votes the presentation frame rate on the
+    video Surface (``ANativeWindow_setFrameRate``, seamless-only), so the
+    compositor can match the display refresh; deliberate display-mode
+    switches remain the embedder's job.
+
 ``mediacodec_embed`` (Android)
     Renders ``IMGFMT_MEDIACODEC`` frames directly to an ``android.view.Surface``.
     Requires ``--hwdec=mediacodec`` for hardware decoding, along with
